cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "δSnowSac: learning parameters of NOAA's operational Snow-17 and SAC-SMA models through unmodified Fortran"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Kamlesh
    family-names: Sawadekar
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-9011-5399"
repository-code: "https://github.com/kasProg/dsnowsac"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  A neural network learns the parameters of NOAA's operational Snow-17
  snowmelt and SAC-SMA soil-moisture models across many basins at once.
  Both models are unmodified Fortran, wrapped as composed Tesseract
  containers with finite-difference gradients, and trained end to end on
  CAMELS streamflow.
keywords:
  - hydrology
  - differentiable modeling
  - hybrid modeling
  - snowmelt
  - streamflow
  - Tesseract
  - Fortran
